"""Deli Counter 0.246.0 (the factory's roadmap 148): a room counts only what stands on its own storey.

`level_design._room_volume_count` -- what a room already holds, so furnish tops it up rather than doubling it -- asked
`abs(z - (floor + size_z / 2)) < sh`, a foot anywhere between the storey below's floor and the storey above's with both
ends open. A piece standing on either of those floors is exactly `sh` from this one, so whether it counted was float
rounding: 740 volumes in 195 rooms of 55 specs sat in that window, each a piece the room it was counted in went
without. Now a volume counts when its foot is on this storey's floor, to a slab's tolerance, up to the next storey's.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has
been worked out: `level_design.py` (anchored hunks); the 44 specs the rule refurnishes, carried whole; the new
`test_room_count_storey.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone
(`patches/dc_room_count/gen_dc_room_count.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run
refused (`patches/dc_room_count/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_room_count.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
